OL,3,GNEWSAMan who shared beheading videos
OL,4,Ajailed
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who shared videos of prisoners
OL,7,Fbeing beheaded has been jailed for
OL,8,Feight years.
OL,10,FMohammed Malik, 24 and from Burnt Oak
OL,11,FTerrace, Gillingham, Kent, shared the
OL,12,Ffootage across a number of social media
OL,13,Fplatforms.
OL,15,FHe was sentenced at Winchester Crown
OL,16,FCourt on Monday, after being convicted
OL,17,Fof two counts of disseminating a
OL,18,Fterrorist publication and two counts of
OL,19,Fexpression of support for a proscribed
OL,20,Forganisation on 10 April.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
